o write the entire JSON object: {\"implementation\":\"<escaped code>\"}. I'll put it all together. No trailing spaces.\n\nLet me write the escaped Python code more carefully, ensuring all newlines are `\\n`. I'll write each line and then join with `\\n`. But I'll produce a string:\n\ndef solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances_list = case['distances']\\n    dist_dict = {}\\n    for u, v, d in distances_list:\\n        key = (u, v) if u <= v else (v, u)\\n        dist_dict[key] = d\\n    edges = []\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\\n            u = nodes[i]\\n            v = nodes[j]\\n            key = (u, v) if u <= v else (v, u)\\n            d = dist_dict[key]\\n            w = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n            edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1 and n > 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected\\\")\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\n\nNow, in this string, the double quotes inside `raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\")` and in the dict keys need to be escaped with backslash. So I replace the \" characters with \\\" in those places. So the string becomes:\n\n... raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected\\\") ... return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\n\nAlso I need to escape any backslash that might appear in the code? None.\n\nSo the final escaped code string (for JSON value) is as I wrote (with the double quotes escaped). But note: In my above representation, I already used `\\\"` to represent escaped double quotes. In the actual JSON string, I need to write `\\\"` as two characters: backslash and double quote. So in the text, I will write that exactly.\n\nNow I'll construct the JSON object string:\n\n{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances_list = case['distances']\\n    dist_dict = {}\\n    for u, v, d in distances_list:\\n        key = (u, v) if u <= v else (v, u)\\n        dist_dict[key] = d\\n    edges = []\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\\n            u = nodes[i]\\n            v = nodes[j]\\n            key = (u, v) if u <= v else (v, u)\\n            d = dist_dict[key]\\n            w = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n            edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n   